module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_record_literal_naming_a_union_type_is_accepted_at_typecheck

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { FoundAtAmbiguous, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_record_literal_naming_a_union_type_is_accepted_at_typecheck: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_record_literal_naming_a_union_type_is_accepted_at_typecheck" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: FoundAtAmbiguous },

  receipts: [
    "**a record literal whose NAME resolves to a declaration carrying no record constructor -- a coproduct -- is accepted at typecheck**, and the value it builds has no constructor to be: the refusal arrives later, and somewhere else, as a non-exhaustive pattern match at EVAL (INVALID STATE: `type U = A { x: Int } | B` and a data binding `u: U = U { x: 1 }` compile with 0 blocking diagnostics; DESIGN section 4b, `values inhabit declared types`, says the program cannot mean anything, and no typecheck diagnostic says so).",

    "HARM: THIS IS THE COMPILER FLOOR, NOT A DIAGNOSTICS GAP. DESIGN section 4b names `values inhabit declared types` among the floor properties whose failure is a below-baseline regression. A value was built under a type name that has no such constructor, was carried through resolve, infer, emit and realization, and was judged only when a `match` happened to read it. The authoring wall and the judgment were 6 commits and one instrument apart, and the instrument was on main.",

    "SPECIMEN, END TO END: extdeps.systemd.systemd_run `SystemdRunProperty` was a record (`{ property: SystemdUnitProperty, value: NonEmptyStr }`) until gunbc#13942 turned it into the union `NamedUnitSetting { property: SystemdUnitProperty, value: NonEmptyStr } | EmptyCapabilityBoundingSet`. gunbc#14149 then wrote the OLD record shape -- `stop_observation: SystemdRunProperty { property: MemoryMax, value: \"infinity\" }` -- inside a forged-source string in the claim `test.claim.compute_unit_stop_observation_witness`. It was accepted at authoring, merged green against its own base, and refused only at EVAL on main as a NON-EXHAUSTIVE PATTERN MATCH: instrument //gunbc/instruments:compute-run-unit-cold, run 38905139153. The site is fixed at gunbc#14184; THIS row is about the compiler, not the site.",

    "WHY THE CHANGE OF KIND SLIPPED THROUGH: #13942 changed a declaration's KIND, and nothing downstream was retyped -- #14149's claim exercises `compute_stop_observation_properties`, which returns `List<SystemdUnitProperty>`, so no consumer ever put the new union type under judgment. A change of kind is a change to every construction of that name, and there was no wall that asks a construction that question. The base's own green was true: against the base the literal was legal, because the name DID carry a record constructor there. Green on the base plus red on main is not the author's error and not the reviewer's; it is the missing question.",

    "MEASURED AT v1 SEED, SIX ACCEPTED SHAPES, 0 BLOCKING DIAGNOSTICS each, on the pre-fix head 6b71cf72c55 through gunbc.compile_census_probe: a data binding, an fn return, a `List<U>` element, a call argument, a literal MISSING a field of its first arm, and a literal carrying a field NO arm declares. So the wall cannot be reached by tightening the field walk -- four of the six were complete and correct against the arm the field walk was reading. THE FIELD WALK WAS THE PROBLEM: it read the union's CHILD VARIANTS as if they were its fields, which is why a complete arm fit and a bogus field name did not refuse.",

    "WHERE IT REFUSES NOW AND WHY THAT IS THE EARLIEST BOUNDARY: v1.compiler.infer `record_lit_name_declares_union`, asked of the declaration THIS MODULE BINDS THE NAME TO -- `lookup_binding_on_chain` (the module's own declarations, then the names it imports BY NAME), the route record-literal widening already consumes, NEVER the corpus-wide pool walk -- and asked of the resolved EXPANSION (so `type T = U` is judged by what U is, not by the spelling T), BEFORE the field walk, located at the literal's NAME span, naming the variants the author could have meant. Resolve is not earlier for this question: resolve refuses UNRESOLVED names, and this name resolves -- to a coproduct, which is the answer, not an error. Parse cannot ask it: parse has no declarations. Emit is later than the authoring moment and its refusals do not reach the author's editor.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS, THE ADJACENT ROWS THIS IS NOT. `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_coproduct_arm_without_a_constructor_name_is_accepted` is the DUAL and is NOT this row: there the author writes a CONSTRUCTOR NAME where no such arm is declared, and the wall is `check_variant_constructor_name`. Here the author writes a TYPE NAME that exists and is well-formed, and asks it to be a constructor -- the name is real, which is exactly why the unresolved-name refusals stay silent. `variant_arm_position_admits_a_type_name` is the same shape at the arm-declaration site (a type name in `A | B`); this is the construction site. `zero_field_construction_escapes_the_field_set_check` is about a construction supplying NO fields against a declaration that declares some; here the construction may supply every field of an arm and still be uninhabiting, because there is no record to be complete for.",

    "THE RESOLUTION IS THE HARDER HALF, AND IT WAS MEASURED WRONG FIRST. The first cut asked the question of `lookup_type_by_name`, which falls through the module's chain into the global-bare overlay; on current main that refused TWO LEGAL constructions in `test.claim.workspace_commissioning_apply_readback_witness` -- the arm `UnitPropertyRead { value }` of `runner_microvm_slot_start`'s union `UnitPropertyReading`, imported by name from its owner -- because the pool independently declares `type UnitPropertyRead = UnitPropertyValue | UnitPropertyUnreadable` at `live_deploy/unit_standing.dag`, a module the witness never imports. A wall that asks a BINDING question of a SPELLING lookup turns every arm whose name collides with an unrelated union elsewhere into a refusal: the same defect one level up, since the harm this row files is precisely a construction judged against a declaration the author never named. The positive control that catches it is `an_imported_variant_name_is_accepted_under_a_pool_collision` (three modules: the arm owner, an unrelated union authored UNDER THE ARM'S NAME, a consumer importing the first and not the second); an arm whose name resolves inside its owner is accepted even when it carries fields.",

    "THE REASON IS MINTED, NOT BORROWED: `CompilerDiagnostic::TypeNameCarriesNoRecordConstructor`. `VariantNotFound` was refused because it carries a `parent_enum` field, and synthesizing a value for a field the author never wrote fabricates structure (DESIGN section 5). `DeclaredTypeNotInhabited` was refused because it would give one name two meanings (DESIGN section 3, a fork is consolidated later, so a meaning fork is a correctness concern). The new arm's message names the type, lists its variants, and cites the floor property.",

    "IT IS PREPENDED INTO THE DIAGNOSTIC CONCAT, NEVER RETURNED EARLY. An early return absorbed the `TypeMismatch` that `test.claim.compute_unit_stop_observation_witness` claims for the same forged source (its `blocking_class_census(source: forged_raw_property_source, wanted_class: \"TypeMismatch\") holds: fn(n) { n > 0 })`), so a fix that returned would have converted one floor failure into a witness failure -- a refusal that deletes another refusal is a second, quieter way of not judging.",

    "CONTROLS, SO THE WALL IS NOT A WALL ON AUTHORING: both arms constructed the way the declaration says (`A { fields }` and the bare empty arm), a record, and an alias of a record, are ACCEPTED with 0 of this class and 0 blocking in total; an UNRESOLVED name keeps its own diagnostic and gains none of this class (so the population the refusal fires on is exactly `a name that resolves to a coproduct`). The discriminating red is `test.claim.record_literal_names_a_union_type_witness`, whose fixtures are the six accepted shapes above; the message text itself is asserted by name in `record_literal_names_a_union_type_refusal_test`, because a refusal whose reason is not stated is a refusal an author cannot act on.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: a typed, located, blocking diagnostic at the authoring moment, at the name the author wrote, naming the constructors that exist -- and RE-DERIVABLE: the claim module calls the same census builtin the admitted probes use, so the wall is executed by the floor plans rather than asserted in this row. CEILING: no wall yet asks the same question of a name reaching a construction position through an expression whose type was never spelled, or of a construction built through a builtin or Rust binding whose declaration is not in the corpus; those stay unjudged, and a claim of `all uninhabiting constructions refuse` would be false.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the refusal is asked of a NAME in literal position. The rung above it asks it of a VALUE flowing into a position typed by a union with no literal at all -- the constructor question without a spelling to point at -- which is the same floor property (`a value inhabits its declared type`) with no name to locate, and needs a carrier that can point at a flow rather than a token.",

    "v2 IS OUT OF THIS ROW'S SCOPE AND MEASURED SEPARATELY: at head the v2 frontend refuses the same shape EARLIER, at resolve (`resolve_reason_unbound_symbol`), so the v2 corpus never reached the inference question; and the v2 consumer that treats `ConstructNotARecord` as silence -- a refusal arm that evaluates an empty list -- is filed apart, because a refusal arm turned into silence is a different harm than a missing refusal.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
